      "content": "Spread Operator"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Consider this code:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "content": "1const fruits1 = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"kiwi\"];\n2\n3// Use spread operator\n4const fruits2 = [\"orange\", \"mango\", ...fruits1, \"apricot\", \"papaya\"];\n5\n6console.log(fruits2);"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "[\n  'orange', 'mango',\n  'apple',  'banana',\n  'kiwi',   'apricot',\n  'papaya'\n]"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "As you can see, we achieved the result with just one line of code and without multiple method calls."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The spread operator makes adding elements simpler, more readable, and easier to maintain."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In this lesson, you'll learn how the spread operator works and how you can use it to perform different operations."
    },
    {
